      en: "The National Pantheon in Santo Domingo is a former Jesuit monastery built in 1714. It now serves as a mausoleum for the Dominican Republic's national heroes. The building is a Baroque masterpiece with an impressive facade and interior adorned with marble and frescoes. It holds the remains of figures such as Juan Pablo Duarte, the father of the nation. The Pantheon is a place of national reverence and used for state ceremonies. Its architecture reflects the country's religious and political history.",
