      en: "Máximo Gómez National Cemetery in Santiago is the final resting place of many of the Dominican Republic's most prominent figures. Established in 1922, it covers 6 hectares and contains over 5,000 graves. The cemetery features a central monument to Máximo Gómez, a 16-meter obelisk. Among those buried here are presidents, generals, and poets. The cemetery is known for its elaborate marble tombs and sculptures. It is a national monument and a site of annual remembrance ceremonies.",
